    "body": "Potential fix for [https://github.com/lkminiPhantomWorld/welcome/security/code-scanning/2](https://github.com/lkminiPhantomWorld/welcome/security/code-scanning/2)\n\nAdd an explicit `permissions` block to the workflow file so the token is restricted to least privilege.  \nBest fix here: set top-level workflow permissions to read-only for repository contents, which is sufficient for `actions/checkout` and the current lint/test steps.\n\n**File to change:** `.github/workflows/python-package-conda.yml`  \n**Change location:** near the top of the workflow, after the `on:` trigger and before `jobs:`.  \n**Exact change:** add:\n```yml\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n```\nNo imports, methods, or dependencies are needed.\n\n\n_Suggested fixes powered by Copilot Autofix. Review carefully before merging._\n",
